 the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we denote our number by $k,$ then the phrase can be written as $\\frac{2}{3}k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c85dc72-0610-5247-b0e6-19c3a9eb7592"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c85dc72-0610-5247-b0e6-19c3a9eb7592" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c85dc72-0610-5247-b0e6-19c3a9eb7592" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-e173d668-26b8-54ef-9b99-6f55c7ae4f78" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e173d668-26b8-54ef-9b99-6f55c7ae4f78"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e173d668-26b8-54ef-9b99-6f55c7ae4f78" :answer/id #uuid "e173d668-26b8-54ef-9b99-6f55c7ae4f78" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2k}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-5efd65b1-9dc8-5a12-83d6-fd8f864d64db" :question/id #uuid "5efd65b1-9dc8-5a12-83d6-fd8f864d64db" :question/math-academy-id "q-21264" :question/problem "Translate the phrase \"one-quarter of a number minus three-sevenths of another number\" into an algebraic expression." :question/worked-solution "If we denote our first number by $x$ and our second number by $y$, then we can write \"one-quarter of a number \" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x\n$$\n\nand \"three-sevenths of a second number\" as\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$\n\nSo, the whole sentence is \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{3}{7}y.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-25f9fbc9-ce9a-5697-a517-9791b935a1d7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-25f9fbc9-ce9a-5697-a517-9791b935a1d7" :answer-field/id #uuid "25f9fbc9-ce9a-5697-a517-9791b935a1d7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c18e997d-0312-5a04-bb53-c55b706f830a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c18e997d-0312-5a04-bb53-c55b706f830a" "answer-43f95ef4-a07d-56e1-83a5-99f832e76e80" "answer-782a2f51-5196-5bca-8eb9-cd583c54f0eb" "answer-3468384a-6f60-5d04-8eeb-ade9d4813b73" "answer-2a061b4e-158c-520a-b680-e0da5839969a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c18e997d-0312-5a04-bb53-c55b706f830a" :answer/id #uuid "c18e997d-0312-5a04-bb53-c55b706f830a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}x-\\frac{3}{7}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43f95ef4-a07d-56e1-83a5-99f832e76e80" :answer/id #uuid "43f95ef4-a07d-56e1-83a5-99f832e76e80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}x-\\frac{3}{4}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-782a2f51-5196-5bca-8eb9-cd583c54f0eb" :answer/id #uuid "782a2f51-5196-5bca-8eb9-cd583c54f0eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}x+\\frac{1}{4}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3468384a-6f60-5d04-8eeb-ade9d4813b73" :answer/id #uuid "3468384a-6f60-5d04-8eeb-ade9d4813b73" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}x-\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2a061b4e-158c-520a-b680-e0da5839969a" :answer/id #uuid "2a061b4e-158c-520a-b680-e0da5839969a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{7}y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-e410a5c3-45c2-5472-8881-f44191caa0a7" :question/id #uuid "e410a5c3-45c2-5472-8881-f44191caa0a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-184026" :question/problem "Translate the following phrase into an algebraic expression: \"The quotient of twenty and a number.\"\n\nUse the letter $h$ to represent the unknown number.\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "If we denote our number by $h,$ we can write \"the quotient of twenty and a number\" as $\\frac{20}{h}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-95ecba06-df0e-5a8e-b830-79b72e439694"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-95ecba06-df0e-5a8e-b830-79b72e439694" :answer-field/id #uuid "95ecba06-df0e-5a8e-b830-79b72e439694" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-412e16b1-8ba1-5a29-bbd9-ec7f116405e2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-412e16b1-8ba1-5a29-bbd9-ec7f116405e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-412e16b1-8ba1-5a29-bbd9-ec7f116405e2" :answer/id #uuid "412e16b1-8ba1-5a29-bbd9-ec7f116405e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{20}{h}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180773 :tutorial/content "In algebra, there are many different ways to represent multiplication. The following expressions all mean \"two times $y$\":\n\n$$\n2y,\\qquad 2 \\cdot y,\\qquad 2 \\times y.\n$$\n\nWhen a number is next to a variable, it means that we multiply them together. We can also represent multiplication using the dot symbol ($\\cdot$) or the familiar \"times\" symbol ($\\times$), though we tend to avoid using the ($\\times$) symbol because it looks a lot like the variable $x.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186180774 :tutorial/content "The **quotient** of two numbers means that we need to divide the first number by the second number.\n\nFor example, \"the quotient of $x$ and two\" means the same thing as \"$x$ divided by two\" and can be written as either expression below:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x}{2} ,\\qquad x \\div 2 \\, .\n$$\n\nIn algebra, we prefer to represent division using the fraction bar instead of the ($\\div$) symbol." :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179872 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
